  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR adds the K7 law suite of the path kernel (#4027). It joins the existing directory suite `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/` (the binary `laws`, made by #4055 / PR #4123). It adds no new top-level test file.\n\n- One generic check for each law of #4023: L1 to L7 and the link rule. Each check is a function over the stage traits (`GuidePlanner`, `OrderPlanner`, `LoadPlanner`, `LinkProof`, `EntryPlanner`) and the stage outputs of one run. It returns a `LawVerdict`: the law, held or broken, the place, the point, the measured value and the limit.\n- `kit.rs` runs the five planners of a kind on a case (a region stage, a recipe, a stock, the planner's own stock reader) into a `Plan`.\n- `grid.rs` is a stock grid that the checks own. It is separate from the planner's stock reader. It walks the plan step by step. It reads each entry descent and each cut on the stock as it is at that step. It reads the engagement from the contact angle of the cutting edge.\n- `standins.rs` holds stand-in planners that obey each law. Each law file holds one or more planners that break its law in a named way.\n- `registry.rs` holds the 16 phase-1 kinds. Each kind has the state \"not on the kernel yet\". The table is the progress list of the migration. A kind that moves sets its row to `Moved` and registers its recipe. Then `each_moved_kind_obeys_every_law` runs all eight checks on it. The kind writes no new law test.\n\nNo change in `crates/pathkernel/src`: each law can be checked through the public API. No change in a planner. No new dependency. No xtask change.\n\n## The mutation proof\n\n| Law | Obeying stand-in (the check holds) | Breaking stand-in | What the check reports |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L1 | `RingGuide`, and a second `RingGuide` as a shared guide: 0.000 | `Drifting` (hidden state) | \"the loops permuted and restarted\", 0.255 against 0.001 |\n| L1 | | `Seam` (reads the start of the first loop) | \"the loops permuted and restarted\", 0.707 |\n| L1 | | the guide of another kind with the same choice (stepover +0.05) | \"shared guide 0\", 0.636 |\n| L2 | `square_region` and `SideOrder` | `blind_region` (the centre ignores the material side) | \"Inside and Outside centres differ by 0.0000 mm2\" |\n| L2 | | `MaterialOrder` (the order reads the material side) | \"order, start side Inside: the material side changed\", 10.18 |\n| L3 | `SideOrder` for Auto, Inside and Outside: 0.000 | `SideMoves` moves the curves 0.1 mm for Outside | \"ordered set, Auto against Outside\", 0.100 |\n| L3 | | `SideMoves` drops one curve for Outside | \"10 curves against 9\", inf |\n| L4 | the asked stages; `RowsAsRings` with a named fallback | `RowsAsRings` with no fallback | \"guide: 10 curves of another family than asked\", 10 |\n| L4 | | `RampInstead` (a ramp where a helix was asked) | \"entry 0: used Ramp, asked Helix\", 1 |\n| L5 | `ProvedEntry` (a helix with an `IntoMaterial` proof); `NoEntry` (a refusal with a reason) | `ClaimsFree` (an air proof on material) | \"entry 0: material share 1.000\", limit 0.02 |\n| L5 | | `ClaimsFree` (a cleared-column proof on material) | \"entry 0: material share 1.000\" |\n| L6 | `ReadLoad` on the square pocket and on the pocket with an island | `ReadLoad { blind }` (reads a slot as a side cut) | \"cut 0: ae/D 0.987, named: false\", cap 0.625 |\n| L7 | the same output: 0.000 | `RingGuide { extra: 0.01 }` (a moved ring) | \"cut 0 (k 9)\", 0.127 |\n| L7 | | another direction (Conventional) | \"cut 9 (k 0)\", 22.6 |\n| L7 | | no recorded old output | \"the case has no recorded old output\", inf |\n| Link rule | `StraightLink`: 0 lifts on the square pocket | `BadLink::Silent` (a lift that the tally does not count) | \"lifts: 7 in the plan, 0 in the tally\" |\n| Link rule | | `BadLink::Always` (lifts on a fixture with no split ring) | \"lifts on a fixture with no split ring\", 9 |\n| Link rule | | `BadLink::Across` (stays at depth across the island) | \"a crossing out of the area\" at (15, 15), 7.0 |\n\nThe check also found a defect in a stand-in. The first stand-in load planner read too low at the corners of sharp offset rings: the check read ae/D 0.75 against the limit 0.5. The stand-in now names the corners.\n\n## The registry\n\n| Kind | State |\n|---|---|\n| Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive, 2D Offset, Engrave, V-Carve, 2D Chamfer | not on the kernel yet |\n| Circular, Slot, Trochoidal slot, Trace, Slot Undercut, Thread, Bore, 3D Pocket | not on the kernel yet |\n\nThe test `a_kind_marked_as_moved_registers_a_recipe` fails with a message if a row is `Moved` with no recipe, or has a recipe and is not `Moved`. The test `the_registry_guard_names_a_moved_kind_without_a_recipe` proves the guard. The test `the_law_runner_passes_a_registered_kind_that_obeys_every_law` runs the stand-ins through the same path as a moved kind.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/4027-kernel-law-suite.md`. In short:\n\n- The suite is the existing directory suite `laws`. The issue text (\"an existing directory suite\") and the K0 record (`crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/`) agree, because #4055 made that suite.\n- The stage-level laws are here. The toolpath-level readings (lifts, crossings, entries, engagement, fallbacks, old against new) are in PR #4167 (#4154), in the tests of `camcraft-motion`. The kernel crate must not depend on motion. At the switch-over, point 1 of the proof is this suite green for each row, and point 2 is the #4154 readings table.\n- The suite builds a `PlanarRegion` in `kit::rebuild` and `standins::pocket_region`. K1 (#4025) changes `PlanarRegion::new`. The PR of #4025 or #4027 that merges second takes `git merge origin/side/path-kernel` and fixes the two calls.\n- Known limit for K5: the entry stage has no channel to name a fallback (`EntryPlanner::entry` returns `Result<Entry, Refusal>`). Today `check_l4` reports an entry into material of another kind than the asked one as a breach.\n\n## Tests and gates (head of this PR)\n\n- Pinning tests: the 31 new tests in `laws` (`l1_guide::*` .. `link_rule::*`, `registry::*`). The `laws` binary: 64 passed, 0.26 s.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6 cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel`: 1 step (`pathkernel suites: laws`), green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-pathkernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 of 6 steps green (run on 1db488923; the merge of `side/path-kernel` after it adds no pathkernel source change).\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: not run, because no gate list changed.\n- The example catalog suites: not run, because no post and no toolpath changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Depth per point: all fixtures are flat.\n- Arcs, open curves and `Incomplete` verdicts in a full run.\n- The exit lead-out.\n- The record's fixtures (the dog bone of #3741, the disc of #3934, the narrow neck, the open-side band). They join with the first kind that moves.\n- The rule \"full-width cuts outside a named slot = 0\" under `LoadControl::None` (the limit is 1, so `Controlled` cannot name a full-width cut).\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #4027\n",
